IMPORT prelude
IMPORT daydate
IMPORT `ita-types`

-- Income Tax Act 1947 — PART 6: WHAT CAPITAL ALLOWANCES ARE MADE?
--
-- Machinery and plant: initial and annual allowances (s 19, Sixth Schedule),
-- accelerated write-offs (s 19A), balancing allowances and charges (s 20), the
-- order of set-off (s 22A) and carry-forward with the shareholder test (s 23).
-- Industrial buildings (ss 16-18B: expenditure before 23 February 2010), land
-- intensification (s 18C), IP rights (s 19B), cost-sharing (s 19C), IRUs
-- (s 19D) and the special sales and transfers of ss 24-25 are carried in the
-- coverage table; their allowance is an input to the allowances total.
--
-- Source: ../source/ITA1947.txt lines 13588-16643, 35043-35119.

§ `Part 6 — capital allowances`

§§ `Sixth Schedule — working life of machinery and plant`

DECLARE `Asset class` IS ONE OF
    `aircraft`, `bank vaults`, `building and construction equipment`, `cable cars and equipment`
    `cables and related assets`, `containers`, `utility plant`, `electrical equipment`, `electronic equipment`
    `equipment for personal and professional services`, `farming equipment`, `fire safety device`
    `floating and dry docks`, `gas cylinders`, `manufacturing and industrial processing plant and machinery`
    `materials and passenger handling equipment`, `motion picture films`, `musical instruments`
    `office furniture and fixtures`, `office data handling equipment`, `office telecommunication equipment`
    `plant for recreation and amusement`, `railway wagons, lines and equipment`
    `buses`, `business service passenger vehicles`, `taxis`, `trucks, lorries, trailers and vans`, `motor cycles and bicycles`
    `vessels, barges, tugs and similar`, `wholesale and retail trade service assets`

@ref Sixth Schedule
GIVEN a IS AN `Asset class`
GIVETH A NUMBER
`the working life in years of` a MEANS
    CONSIDER a
    WHEN `aircraft`                                                     THEN 5    -- item 1
    WHEN `bank vaults`                                                  THEN 16   -- 2
    WHEN `building and construction equipment`                          THEN 6    -- 3
    WHEN `cable cars and equipment`                                     THEN 12   -- 4
    WHEN `cables and related assets`                                    THEN 16   -- 5
    WHEN `containers`                                                   THEN 10   -- 6
    WHEN `utility plant`                                                THEN 16   -- 7
    WHEN `electrical equipment`                                         THEN 8    -- 8
    WHEN `electronic equipment`                                         THEN 8    -- 9
    WHEN `equipment for personal and professional services`             THEN 10   -- 10
    WHEN `farming equipment`                                            THEN 8    -- 11
    WHEN `fire safety device`                                           THEN 10   -- 12
    WHEN `floating and dry docks`                                       THEN 16   -- 13
    WHEN `gas cylinders`                                                THEN 16   -- 14
    WHEN `manufacturing and industrial processing plant and machinery`  THEN 6    -- 15
    WHEN `materials and passenger handling equipment`                   THEN 6    -- 16
    WHEN `motion picture films`                                         THEN 5    -- 17
    WHEN `musical instruments`                                          THEN 10   -- 18
    WHEN `office furniture and fixtures`                                THEN 10   -- 19(a)
    WHEN `office data handling equipment`                               THEN 8    -- 19(b)
    WHEN `office telecommunication equipment`                           THEN 10   -- 19(c)
    WHEN `plant for recreation and amusement`                           THEN 10   -- 20
    WHEN `railway wagons, lines and equipment`                          THEN 16   -- 21
    WHEN `buses`                                                        THEN 6    -- 22(a)
    WHEN `business service passenger vehicles`                          THEN 6    -- 22(b)
    WHEN `taxis`                                                        THEN 5    -- 22(c)
    WHEN `trucks, lorries, trailers and vans`                           THEN 6    -- 22(d)
    WHEN `motor cycles and bicycles`                                    THEN 8    -- 22(e)
    WHEN `vessels, barges, tugs and similar`                            THEN 16   -- 23
    WHEN `wholesale and retail trade service assets`                    THEN 8    -- 24

§§ `Initial and annual allowances (s 19)`

-- s 19(1): an initial allowance "equal to one-fifth of that expenditure" for
-- the YA of the basis period in which it is incurred. s 19(2)(a): for an asset
-- acquired before the basis period for YA 2023, the annual allowance is the
-- original cost less the initial allowance, divided by the working life in the
-- Sixth Schedule. (2)(bb): for an asset acquired in the basis period for YA
-- 2023 or later, divided instead by the number of years the person elects: 6 or
-- 12 where the working life is less than 16; 6, 12 or 16 where it is 16.
-- (2)(bc): the election is irrevocable.
@ref s 19(1)
GIVEN cost IS A NUMBER
GIVETH A NUMBER
`the s 19 initial allowance on` cost MEANS cost DIVIDED BY 5

@ref s 19(2)(a), (bb)
GIVEN cost            IS A NUMBER
      class           IS AN `Asset class`
      `YA acquired`   IS A NUMBER
      `years elected` IS A NUMBER
GIVETH A NUMBER
`the s 19 annual allowance on` cost `, class` class `, acquired for YA` `YA acquired` `, years elected` `years elected` MEANS
    IF   `YA acquired` LESS THAN 2023
    THEN `the base` DIVIDED BY `the working life in years of` class                                           -- (a)
    ELSE IF `a permitted election`
         THEN `the base` DIVIDED BY `years elected`                                                           -- (bb)
         ELSE REFUSE "s 19(2)(bb): the years elected must be 6 or 12 (or 16 for a 16-year asset)"
    WHERE
        `the base` MEANS cost MINUS `the s 19 initial allowance on` cost
        `a permitted election` MEANS
               `years elected` EQUALS 6
            OR `years elected` EQUALS 12
            OR (`years elected` EQUALS 16 AND `the working life in years of` class EQUALS 16)

§§ `Accelerated allowances (s 19A)`

DECLARE `Write-off` IS ONE OF
    `the s 19 initial and annual allowances`
    `s 19A(1) 3-year write-off`                       -- 33⅓% a year
    `s 19A(1E) 2-year write-off`                      -- 75% then 25%, YA 2021, 2022 or 2024 expenditure
    `s 19A(2) computer or prescribed automation, 100%`
    `s 19A(10A) low-value asset, 100%`

-- s 19A(1): "an annual allowance of 33 1/3% in respect of the capital
-- expenditure incurred", (1A) not more than the expenditure unallowed.
-- (1E): for expenditure in the basis period for YA 2021, 2022 or 2024, 75% for
-- that YA and 25% for the next, if elected. (2): computers and prescribed
-- automation equipment, 100% if elected. (10A), (10B): an item costing not
-- more than $5,000, 100% if elected, the aggregate of such allowances in a YA
-- not more than $30,000.
@ref s 19A(1), (1A), (1E), (2)
GIVEN w          IS A `Write-off`
      cost       IS A NUMBER
      `YA incurred` IS A NUMBER
      ya         IS A NUMBER
GIVETH A NUMBER
`the s 19A allowance by` w `on` cost `incurred for YA` `YA incurred` `, for YA` ya MEANS
    CONSIDER w
    WHEN `s 19A(1) 3-year write-off` THEN
        IF ya AT LEAST `YA incurred` AND ya AT MOST `YA incurred` PLUS 2 THEN cost DIVIDED BY 3 ELSE 0
    WHEN `s 19A(1E) 2-year write-off` THEN
        BRANCH IF NOT (`YA incurred` EQUALS 2021 OR `YA incurred` EQUALS 2022 OR `YA incurred` EQUALS 2024)
                  THEN REFUSE "s 19A(1E): only expenditure in the basis period for YA 2021, 2022 or 2024"
               IF ya EQUALS `YA incurred`        THEN cost TIMES 75%
               IF ya EQUALS `YA incurred` PLUS 1 THEN cost TIMES 25%
               OTHERWISE 0
    WHEN `s 19A(2) computer or prescribed automation, 100%` THEN
        IF ya EQUALS `YA incurred` THEN cost ELSE 0
    WHEN `s 19A(10A) low-value asset, 100%` THEN
        BRANCH IF cost GREATER THAN 5000 THEN REFUSE "s 19A(10A): only an item costing not more than $5,000"
               IF ya EQUALS `YA incurred` THEN cost
               OTHERWISE 0
    WHEN `the s 19 initial and annual allowances` THEN
        REFUSE "use the s 19 rules, which need the asset class and the years elected"

@ref s 19A(10B)
GIVEN `low-value claims in the YA` IS A LIST OF NUMBER
GIVETH A NUMBER
`the low-value asset allowances allowed, claims` `low-value claims in the YA` MEANS
    IF sum `low-value claims in the YA` GREATER THAN 30000 THEN 30000 ELSE sum `low-value claims in the YA`

§§ `Balancing allowances and charges (s 20)`

DECLARE `Balancing adjustment` IS ONE OF
    `a balancing allowance` HAS `amount` IS A NUMBER
    `a balancing charge`    HAS `amount` IS A NUMBER
    `no adjustment`

-- s 20(2A): if the sale (insurance, salvage, compensation) moneys are less than
-- the expenditure still unallowed, a balancing allowance of the shortfall. (3):
-- if they exceed it, a balancing charge of the excess. (4): the charge is not
-- more than the allowances made under ss 19 and 19A. (1A), (2): at the
-- open-market price where the asset passes below it or stays with the owner.
@ref s 20(2A), (3), (4)
GIVEN `still unallowed`  IS A NUMBER
      `sale moneys`      IS A NUMBER
      `allowances made`  IS A NUMBER
GIVETH A `Balancing adjustment`
`the balancing adjustment, unallowed` `still unallowed` `, sale moneys` `sale moneys` `, allowances made` `allowances made` MEANS
    BRANCH IF `sale moneys` LESS THAN `still unallowed`
              THEN `a balancing allowance` (`still unallowed` MINUS `sale moneys`)
           IF `sale moneys` GREATER THAN `still unallowed`
              THEN `a balancing charge` (IF `sale moneys` MINUS `still unallowed` GREATER THAN `allowances made` THEN `allowances made` ELSE `sale moneys` MINUS `still unallowed`)
           OTHERWISE `no adjustment`

§§ `Set-off and carry-forward (ss 22A, 23)`

-- s 22A: brought-forward balances are used first, earliest first, then the
-- current YA's allowances. s 23(1): what cannot be used for want of income is
-- carried forward "so long as the person ... continues to carry on the trade".
-- s 23(4), (7): for a company, only if "not less than 50% of the total number of
-- issued shares" are held by the same persons on the last day of the year the
-- allowance arose and on the first day of the YA it would be used, unless
-- exempted under (5) (then (6): only against the same trade).
DECLARE `Allowances used` HAS
    `allowed this YA`        IS A NUMBER
    `carried forward`        IS A NUMBER

@ref ss 22A, 23(1)
GIVEN `brought forward`        IS A NUMBER
      `current allowances`     IS A NUMBER
      `income available`       IS A NUMBER
      `the business continues` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH AN `Allowances used`
`the allowances used, brought forward` `brought forward` `, current` `current allowances` `, against income` `income available` `, business continuing:` `the business continues` MEANS
    `Allowances used` WITH
        `allowed this YA` IS `used`
        `carried forward` IS IF `the business continues` THEN `total` MINUS `used` ELSE 0
    WHERE
        `total` MEANS `brought forward` PLUS `current allowances`
        `used` MEANS IF `total` GREATER THAN `income available` THEN (IF `income available` LESS THAN 0 THEN 0 ELSE `income available`) ELSE `total`

@ref s 23(4)-(7)
GIVEN `percent held by the same persons on both dates` IS A NUMBER
      `exempted by the Minister under s 23(5)`         IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `a company may carry forward allowances, same shareholders holding` `percent held by the same persons on both dates` `, exempted:` `exempted by the Minister under s 23(5)` IF
        `percent held by the same persons on both dates` AT LEAST 50%
    OR  `exempted by the Minister under s 23(5)`
